# M9: IRQControl_GetMSI and an MSI from a device
# (kernel/src/arch/x86_64/m9test.rs). Under TCG there is no Hypervisor
# capability, so slots 12 to 14 are null and GetSint is IllegalOperation.
# GetMSI, made through l4core::invoke on the root task's IRQControl as the
# root task would make it, gives IRQ 0 with the boot CPU's physical, fixed,
# edge message; then all 192 vectors in order, RevokeFirst for GetMSI and
# GetIOAPIC once none is free, and a deleted handler's vector reissued.
# The HPET's last comparator, with FSB delivery (QEMU's hpet.msi), then
# writes GetMSI's data to its address as a device's MSI does: the bound
# notification is signalled, a second message with no Ack signals again,
# and after the handler's deletion a third signals nothing.
cmdline: test=msi
qemu_args: -global hpet.msi=on
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: hyperv: no Hypervisor capability, slots 12 to 14 null: no TLFS interface
expect: msi: ok   no Hypervisor capability under TCG
expect: msi: ok   GetSint(2) is IllegalOperation without a SynIC
expect: msi: ok   GetMSI: IRQ 0, address 0xfee00000 (APIC ID 0), data 0x30
expect: msi: ok   GetMSI 192 times gave IRQs 0 to 191 in order
expect: msi: ok   deleting IRQ 100's handler freed its vector, and GetMSI reissued it
expect: msi: ok   deleting the 191 other handlers freed IRQs 1 to 191
expect: msi: ok   the HPET's FSB message signalled the notification
expect: msi: ok   a second message, with no Ack, signalled again
expect: msi: ok   after the handler's deletion the device's next message landed on a free entry
expect: TEST PASS
forbid: TEST FAIL
